{"symbol":"G1A.DE","area":"europe","updated":"2026-11-09T20:09:28Z","info":{"address1":"Ulmenstrasse 99","city":"Düsseldorf","zip":"40476","country":"Germany","phone":"49 211 9136 0","fax":"49 211 9136 31087","website":"https://www.gea.com","industry":"Specialty Industrial Machinery","industryKey":"specialty-industrial-machinery","industryDisp":"Specialty Industrial Machinery","sector":"Industrials","sectorKey":"industrials","sectorDisp":"Industrials","longBusinessSummary":"GEA Group Aktiengesellschaft produces and supplies systems and components to the food, beverage, and pharmaceutical industries worldwide. The company operates through Separation & Flow Technologies; Liquid & Power Technologies; Food & Health Technologies; Farm Technologies; and Heating & Refrigeration Technologies segments. It manufactures process-related components and machinery, notably separators, decanters, homogenizers, valves, and pumps; and process solutions, including brewing systems, liquid processing and filling, concentration, fermentation, crystallization, purification, drying, powder handling, and packaging, as well as systems for carbon capture and emission control for dairy, new-food, beverage, food, chemical, and other industries. The company also prepares, marinates, and processes meat, poultry, seafood, vegan products, and snack and pasta, as well as slicing, packaging lines, freeze drying, granulators, and tablet presses for pharmaceutical industry. In addition, it offers customer solutions for milk production and livestock farming comprising automatic milking and feeding system, conventional milking solutions, manure handling, and digital herd management tools; and energy solutions in the field of industrial refrigeration and heating for various industries, including food, beverage, dairy, oil and gas, supporting automation, digital, and service platform. The company was formerly known as mg technologies ag and changed its name to GEA Group Aktiengesellschaft in 2005. GEA Group Aktiengesellschaft was founded in 1881 and is headquartered in Düsseldorf, Germany.","fullTimeEmployees":19804,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Stefan  Klebert Dipl.-Ing., MBA","age":60,"title":"CEO & Chairman of the Executive Board","yearBorn":1965,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":3195694,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Alexander  Kocherscheidt","age":52,"title":"CFO & Member of Executive Board","yearBorn":1973,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":866129,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Kai  Becker","age":44,"title":"Division CEO of Pure Flow Processing & Member of Executive Board","yearBorn":1981,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Dr. Nadine  Sterley","age":45,"title":"Chief People & Sustainability Officer, Labour Director and Member of Executive Board","yearBorn":1980,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Peter  Lauwers","age":55,"title":"Division CEO of Pharma & Food Applications and Member of Executive Board","yearBorn":1970,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Klaus  Stojentin","age":58,"title":"Division CEO of Nutrition Plant Engineering & Member of Executive Board","yearBorn":1967,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Oliver  Luckenbach","title":"Head of Investor Relations","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Jill  Meiburg","title":"Head of Corporate Communications, Marketing and Brand","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Ilija  Aprcovic","title":"Chief Executive Officer of Liquid & Powder Technologies Business","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Dr. Andreas  Seeringer","title":"Division Chief Executive Officer of FarmTechnologies","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedVa